> Check CRD shuffle with supplied channel indices

SRGAN packs output channels as c*r*r+dy*r+dx. For two channels and scale2,
packed indices0..7 become spatial pixels(0,4),(1,5),(2,6),(3,7), in row-major
pixel order. The native shuffle uses reshape/transpose, with live gradients.
It does not interchange the channel and subpixel axes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_shuffle_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto x      = n::reshape(n::arange(0, 8, 1, n::DType::Float64), {1, 1, 1, 8}).requires_grad_();
  auto y      = n::models::SRPixelShuffle(x, 2, 2);
  if (y.to_vector<double>() != std::vector<double>{0, 4, 1, 5, 2, 6, 3, 7})
    throw std::runtime_error("source CRD order");
  auto matrix = n::reshape(y, {4, 2});
  auto p      = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-.5, 11)
      .points(
          {0, 1, 2, 3}, n::select(matrix, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(), "Channel0", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .points(
          {0, 1, 2, 3}, n::select(matrix, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(), "Channel1", {220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .x_label("Output spatial pixel, row-major order")
      .y_label("Supplied packed input-channel index")
      .title("CRD keeps each channel's four subpixels together")
      .save_svg("build/asr_shuffle_toy.svg");
}
```
