> Capture BN moments before writing weights, then commit them explicitly

SRGAN normalizes with live population moments in its training path, while
saved-statistic inference reads detached moving values. Five layers capture
four-channel means and source-rounded unbiased variances. Captures are detached
and do not update state. After the G weight write, the caller commits
old*double(float32(.9))+captured*double(1-float32(.9)). Moments must come from
that same pre-write G capture, rather than a recomputed forward after the write.

For supplied values1,3,5,7, batch mean4 and population variance5 produce an
unbiased estimate near20/3. Starting saved mean0/variance1, the candidate mean
is near.4 and variance1.5667. The example shows batch normalization and saved
inference before/after the explicit commit. The reusable primitive itself has
no affine gamma/beta; the SR generator applies its learned affine terms afterward.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_bn_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore stats(0, n::DType::Float64);
  auto              x       = n::tensor({1., 3., 5., 7.}, {4, 1}, stats.dtype());
  auto              capture = n::capture_batch_norm(stats, "toy", x, true);
  auto              before  = n::capture_batch_norm(stats, "toy", x, false).value;
  if (stats.at("toy/moving_mean").item() != 0)
    throw std::runtime_error("capture does not write");
  auto next = n::batch_norm_moving_values(
      stats.at("toy/moving_mean"),
      stats.at("toy/moving_var"),
      capture.mean.detach(),
      capture.unbiased_variance.detach());
  stats.set("toy/moving_mean", next.mean);
  stats.set("toy/moving_var", next.variance);
  auto after = n::capture_batch_norm(stats, "toy", x, false).value;
  auto p     = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-2, 12)
      .points({0, 1, 2, 3}, capture.value.to_vector<double>(), "Live batch", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .points({0, 1, 2, 3}, before.to_vector<double>(), "Saved before", {220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .points({0, 1, 2, 3}, after.to_vector<double>(), "Saved after", {22, 163, 74}, 5)
      .x_label("Supplied observation index")
      .y_label("Normalized value, no learned affine terms")
      .title("Read-only capture and explicit moving-statistic commit are separate")
      .save_svg("build/asr_bn_toy.svg");
}
```
