\image(figures/asr_bn_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Twelve plotted values come from four supplied observations under three moment choices. Five real SRGAN layers follow the same capture/commit protocol; ESRGAN has no BN.)
\alttext(Three four-point series compare live batch normalization with saved statistics before and after an explicit moving update.)

> Retain opposite-pool means in relativistic-average derivatives

[Jolicoeur-Martineau, The relativistic discriminator: a key element missing from
standard GAN (2018)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.00734) motivates comparing real
and generated scores relatively. This source uses rr=real-mean(fake) and
rf=fake-mean(real), with LIVE opposite-pool means. ESRGAN D is
.5*(mean softplus(-rr)+mean softplus(rf)); G reverses both signs, with the same
half. Unequal positive pool sizes are supported by the reusable native loss.
A common score shift cancels up to floating rounding.

The supplied real(-2,0,3),fake(-1,2) fixture compares correct G score partials
with a diagnostic that stops both means. The correct total score partial sums
to zero under a common shift. The stopped-mean control changes the derivatives
while leaving the forward loss unchanged; it is not used during fitting.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_relative_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n  = dm::nn;
  auto t       = n::DType::Float64;
  auto r       = n::tensor({-2., 0., 3.}, {3, 1}, t).requires_grad_(),
       f       = n::tensor({-1., 2.}, {2, 1}, t).requires_grad_();
  auto o       = n::models::RelativisticAverageGan(r, f);
  auto correct = n::grad(o.generator, {r, f});
  auto stopped = .5 * (n::mean(n::softplus(r - n::mean(f).detach())) +
                       n::mean(n::softplus(-(f - n::mean(r).detach()))));
  auto wrong   = n::grad(stopped, {r, f});
  if (std::abs(n::sum(correct[0]).item() + n::sum(correct[1]).item()) > 1e-14)
    throw std::runtime_error("common-shift derivative");
  auto flatten = [](const std::vector<n::Tensor>& x) {
    return n::concat({n::reshape(x[0], {-1}), n::reshape(x[1], {-1})}, 0).to_vector<double>();
  };
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-.7, .8)
      .points({0, 1, 2, 4, 5}, flatten(correct), "Live means", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .points({0, 1, 2, 4, 5}, flatten(wrong), "Stopped control", {220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .x_label("Real score coordinates0/1/2, fake coordinates4/5")
      .y_label("G adversarial partial with respect to each supplied score")
      .title("Both cross-pool derivatives are part of the relativistic loss")
      .save_svg("build/asr_relative_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/asr_relative_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All ten score partials compare live versus stopped opposite-pool means. The actual game keeps both means live and supports unequal pool sizes.)
\alttext(Two five-point series compare relativistic generator score partials with a diagnostic stopped-mean control.)

> Trace both native residual generators and the image-only critic

SRGAN uses a fan-in-uniform3→4 head/PReLU, two bias-free convolution/BN/PReLU
residual blocks, body convolution/BN with global head skip, packed4→16 up
convolution, CRD shuffle2 and PReLU. ESRGAN uses three sequential five-conv
blocks, each four growth2 leaky maps followed by a four-channel tail and.2
residual scaling. Its source-specific body input is head+.2*last_block, then
body-tail convolution plus a global head skip, nearest2, up/HR leaky convolutions.
These two source adaptations and the bicubic IMAGE shortcut remain explicit.
Both output kernels use normal(.001), biases zero; other kernels use the
source Float32 fan-in bound. The traces execute the native APIs and verify counts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_srgan_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore g(7001), stats(0);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& lr) {
        auto bic = m::SRBicubic(lr, 32, 32);
        n::model_stage("Bicubic image shortcut", lr, bic);
        auto o = m::AdversarialSRGenerate(g, stats, lr, bic, false, false);
        n::model_stage("Head3 to4", lr, o.head);
        n::model_stage("Two BN residuals and global skip", o.head, o.body);
        n::model_stage("Pack4 to16", o.body, o.packed);
        n::model_stage("CRD shuffle2", o.packed, o.shuffled);
        n::model_stage("Up PReLU4", o.shuffled, o.upsampled);
        n::model_stage("Small output conv4 to3", o.upsampled, o.residual);
        return n::model_stage(
            "Bicubic + image residual", std::vector<n::Tensor>{bic, o.residual}, o.image);
      },
      "SRGAN: unbounded residual over bicubic");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 4;
  auto figure                   = model.plot(n::ones({1, 16, 16, 3}), options);
  if (figure.parameter_count() != 1591 || g.size() != 25 || stats.count() != 40)
    throw std::runtime_error("executed native G census");
  figure.save_svg("build/asr_srgan_architecture.svg");
}
```
