\alttext(An executed LR-to-HR generator trace keeps its image-level bicubic skip, native feature upsampling and small residual output convolution.)

The shared critic architecture is head3→4/leaky.2, two4x4/stride2 maps to8
channels/leaky.2, global spatial mean and raw score1. The ordinary SRGAN score
head is Glorot dense with bias,1673 values/8 leaves. ESRGAN uses a bias-free
8x1 kernel with bound sqrt(6.f/9),1672/7. The trace below executes that relative
variant. Neither critic uses BN or sigmoid.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_critic_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore d(7013);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& image) { return n::models::AdversarialSRDiscriminate(d, image, true); },
      "ESRGAN critic: raw bias-free score after global mean");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Layers;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 4;
  auto f                        = model.plot(n::ones({1, 32, 32, 3}), options);
  if (f.parameter_count() != 1672 || d.size() != 7)
    throw std::runtime_error("relative D census");
  f.save_svg("build/asr_critic_architecture.svg");
}
```
