> Distinguish cumulative writes from optimizer counters after the cold reset

The next plot reads all48 after-G phase counter records for SRGAN. G reaches16
during warm-up, resets to0, then ends at32 after its32 GAN steps. D stays0
during warm-up and also ends32. ESRGAN has the same counter trajectory. The
independent audit reconstructs every Adam transition and confirms that keeping
the warm-up moments instead would change the first GAN G write by up to
.000184068(SRGAN) or.000194842(ESRGAN). A reset itself changes no model values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_reset_counters.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  std::vector<double> x, g, d;
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= 3; ++epoch)
    for (int batch = 0; batch < 16; ++batch) {
      std::string file = "phases/epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + "-batch" + std::to_string(batch) +
                         "-g-iterations.npz";
      auto a = Read("build/srgan_esrgan/srgan/" + file),
           b = Read("build/srgan_esrgan/esrgan/" + file);
      if (!n::equal_bits(a.at("iterations"), b.at("iterations")))
        throw std::runtime_error("same declared counter schedule");
      auto counter = a.at("iterations").to_vector<double>();
      x.push_back(x.size() + 1);
      g.push_back(counter[0]);
      d.push_back(counter[1]);
    }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-2, 52)
      .lines(x, g, "G Adam counter", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(x, d, "D Adam counter", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .x_label("Cumulative generator writes1..48; reset precedes write17")
      .y_label("Actual optimizer iteration counter")
      .title("48 G writes end at counter32 after an explicit cold reset")
      .save_svg("build/asr_reset_counters.svg");
}
```
