> Compare per-image PSNR gains, not just a pooled aggregate

Metrics use the common central20x20 crop, studio-range BT.601 luminance and
clipping of estimated/bicubic luminance into[0,1]. Reference HR luminance is
unclipped. The source reports the mean of32 per-image PSNRs and SSIMs; pooled
PSNR from mean MSE is a different aggregate. SRGAN mean/pooled PSNR are
26.75467688/26.26674257 dB; ESRGAN26.73889463/26.25239098. Bicubic mean is
26.71119211 dB. Mean gains are only.04348477/.02770251 dB. The next plot keeps
all32 per-image gains for each model, including negative improvements.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_psnr_gains.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto                             p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> gain;
  double                           lo = 0, hi = 0;
  for (const std::string name : {"srgan", "esrgan"}) {
    auto a = Read("build/srgan_esrgan/" + name + "/probe-per-image-metrics.npz");
    gain.push_back((a.at("psnr") - a.at("bicubic_psnr")).to_vector<double>());
    for (double v : gain.back()) {
      lo = std::min(lo, v);
      hi = std::max(hi, v);
    }
  }
  auto   x    = n::arange(0, 32, 1, n::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
  double span = std::max(.02, hi - lo);
  p.y_limits(lo - .15 * span, hi + .8 * span)
      .points(x, gain[0], "SRGAN gain", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .points(x, gain[1], "ESRGAN gain", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .x_label("Test row index0..31, source IDs50064..50095")
      .y_label("Per-image PSNR minus bicubic PSNR, dB")
      .title("All32 held-out gains, including losses relative to bicubic")
      .save_svg("build/asr_psnr_gains.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/asr_psnr_gains.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All64 paired per-image gains are retained in original test order. Mean gains are small; this32-image teaching sample does not establish perceptual improvement or benchmark performance.)
\alttext(Two32-point series compare each model PSNR gain against the same per-image bicubic reference.)

SSIM uses a normalized11x11 Gaussian window,sigma1.5,valid centers,
C1=.0001,C2=.0009,population variances clamped at0 against roundoff and signed
covariance. Mean SSIM is.85584107/.85522090 versus bicubic.85413543. The plot
shows every per-image difference multiplied by1000 for readable display units;
it does not drop negative differences or convert them into a quality claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/asr_ssim_gains.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  auto                             p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::vector<std::vector<double>> delta;
  double                           lo = 0, hi = 0;
  for (const std::string name : {"srgan", "esrgan"}) {
    auto a = Read("build/srgan_esrgan/" + name + "/probe-per-image-metrics.npz");
    delta.push_back(((a.at("ssim") - a.at("bicubic_ssim")) * 1000.).to_vector<double>());
    for (double v : delta.back()) {
      lo = std::min(lo, v);
      hi = std::max(hi, v);
    }
  }
  auto   x    = n::arange(0, 32, 1, n::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
  double span = std::max(1., hi - lo);
  p.y_limits(lo - .15 * span, hi + .8 * span)
      .points(x, delta[0], "SRGAN delta", {37, 99, 235}, 4)
      .points(x, delta[1], "ESRGAN delta", {220, 38, 38}, 4)
      .x_label("Same32 test rows in source order")
      .y_label("Per-image SSIM minus bicubic, multiplied by1000")
      .title("Small SSIM changes retain their per-image variation")
      .save_svg("build/asr_ssim_gains.svg");
}
